maria_cs: FYI onboarding with Luminary hitting repeated 429s during SDK setup. They spin up a lot of workers and each worker fetches an ephemeral token at startup. Sample log line: '429 rate_limit exceeded ephemeral_token_window tenant=luminary-inc worker=12'. Need quick mitigation suggestions.

logan_support: Which account/environ? any root request id or a short log snippet would help.

maria_cs: Account: luminary-inc (acct_4839). Logs: '2026-03-16T10:12:03Z ERROR 429 rate_limit exceeded ephemeral_token_window tenant=luminary-inc worker=12 req_id=01F3...'. Happens during CI deploy -> scale to 40-60 workers.

jasper_se: Sounds like a token-rotation stampede. Do they call the token endpoint per worker (no shared cache)? Also can you confirm SDK version?

sumi_eng: yes we currently fetch per worker for simplicity, Node SDK v0.9.1. snippet from our bootstrap: 
```js
// naive worker boot
async function initWorker() {
  const token = await fetch('/get-ephemeral-token'); // each worker does this
  client.init({ token });
}
for (let i = 0; i < 50; i++) { initWorker(); }
```

jasper_se: Ok. Quick remediation checklist: 1) centralize token fetch so only one network call at startup, 2) add startup splay (random delay) to spread requests, 3) add exponential backoff with jitter on token retries. Example patterns: 
```js
let tokenPromise = null;
async function getTokenOnce() {
  if (!tokenPromise) {
    tokenPromise = fetch('/get-ephemeral-token').then(r => r.json());
  }
  return tokenPromise;
}
async function initWorker() {
  // splay startup by up to 1.5s
  await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, Math.random() * 1500));
  const token = await getTokenOnce();
  client.init({ token: token.value });
}

// backoff with jitter
async function retryWithJitter(fn, tries = 5) {
  for (let i = 0; i < tries; i++) {
    try { return await fn(); } catch (e) {
      const wait = Math.pow(2, i) * 100 + Math.random() * 1000;
      await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, wait));
    }
  }
  throw new Error('token fetch failed after retries');
}
```

devon_infra: On infra side, we can also temporarily raise TTL for ephemeral tokens for this tenant so they don't re-request on short restarts. Longer term we have options (queued issuance / warm pool), but TTL bump is fastest.

maria_cs: I'll ask ops to bump ephemeral TTL for luminary-inc (requesting 5m for now). @sumi_eng can you try the splay + shared-token approach in a canary? also reduce startup parallelism if possible.

opsbot: Rate policy note: ephemeral-token-issue window = 120 req/min per tenant. Auto-throttle engages around 90% of that window.

sumi_eng: Trying change now (shared token + splay). Ran a small canary: previously ~30 429s in first minute, now 2 x 429 only. Looks promising, will run a full deploy later. Thanks folks.

maria_cs: :thumbsup: I'll follow up with a short playbook and add a runbook link to onboarding docs. Docs draft: https://redwood.internal/runbooks/token-rotation. Will also confirm TTL bump once ops approves.

jasper_se: If you need a drop-in patch for the SDK, I can PR a Promise-cache + splay helper today.

sumi_eng: Please do, that'd be ideal.

maria_cs: great — assigning follow-up: create tiny playbook + add SDK snippet. Closing triage for now, will reopen if 429s reappear.
